    "description": "An insurance backend integrates a third-party billing system over a SOAP-ish HTTP API. Every service class that needs an invoice today builds its own request URL, parses the response XML inline and repeats the same retry and timeout handling; three of them disagree about how a rejected invoice is reported. The vendor ships breaking changes twice a year, and after the last upgrade four call sites had to be found and fixed by hand. The team wants exactly one component that knows the vendor protocol, translates it into the internal invoice model and back, enforces the timeout and retry policy, and is the only place that has to change when the vendor moves. The decision to implement: how one component owns access to an external system and maps between its foreign representation and the internal model.",
    "decision_statement": "Concentrate access to the external billing system in one component that owns its protocol, mapping and error translation.",
    "notes": "Service-stub and data-transfer-object are the classic alternatives a reviewer may accept for the same seam."
  },
